              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: The QUIC stack queues a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame also for retransmitted NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames. This allows a remote malicious QUIC stack to queue an unlimited number of RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames.  Impact summary: A malicious remote QUIC peer can trigger an out-of-memory condition causing a Denial of Service.  CWE: CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling  Description: The earlier fix for CVE-2026-84784 was not complete. It failed to ignore retransmissions of the NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame. The QUIC implementation created and inserted a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame for every retransmitted NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame it received and there was no limit on how many RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames were queued. This allows a malicious remote QUIC stack to trigger an out-of-memory (OOM) condition.  FIPS impact: no The FIPS module is not affected as the QUIC implementation is outside the OpenSSL FIPS module boundary."
