                "text": "CVE-2026-121758 medium vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Converting crafted ISO-2022-CN-EXT input to UTF-8 character encoding, in the GNU C Library version 2.2 through 2.44 may result in the converter reading past the end of the input buffer, causing the calling application to crash.  When the ISO-2022-CN-EXT decoder encounters an invalid input byte sequence like '\\x0e' it ends up advancing the pointer tracking the read buffer position twice.  If this sequence is at the end of the input buffer, the decoder may then end up reading past the bounds of the input buffer.  To exploit this, the input and encoding needs to be attacker controlled."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-121758",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-121758\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.43-7\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-121758](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-121758)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-121758**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libc-bin  | 2.43-7  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-121758](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-121758)  |\n"
